 ],
 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "You need a railroad, so you lay the steel rails right on the dirt. Problem solved!",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But a train weighs thousands of tons, and the thin rails dig into the ground.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you set the rails on wide crossties, to spread the weight out.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But rain soaks the dirt under the ties, and they sink unevenly. The track goes wavy.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you build the whole track on a thick bed of crushed rock. That's ballast.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Water drains straight through the gaps, so the ground under it stays firm.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "The sharp edges lock together, so the ties can't slide, and weeds can't take root.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "And when the track settles, a machine just packs the rocks back under the ties.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just built a railroad. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.2
  }
 ],
